{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1266, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given an integer array nums of size n. For each index i where 0 <= i < n, define a subarray nums[start ... i] where start = max(0, i - nums[i]).\nReturn the total sum of all elements from the subarray defined for each index in the array.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums = [2,3,1]\nOutput: 11\nExplanation:\n\n\n\ni\nSubarray\nSum\n\n\n0\nnums[0] = [2]\n2\n\n\n1\nnums[0 ... 1] = [2, 3]\n5\n\n\n2\nnums[1 ... 2] = [3, 1]\n4\n\n\nTotal Sum\n \n11\n\n\n\nThe total sum is 11. Hence, 11 is the output.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums = [3,1,1,2]\nOutput: 13\nExplanation:\n\n\n\ni\nSubarray\nSum\n\n\n0\nnums[0] = [3]\n3\n\n\n1\nnums[0 ... 1] = [3, 1]\n4\n\n\n2\nnums[1 ... 2] = [1, 1]\n2\n\n\n3\nnums[1 ... 3] = [1, 1, 2]\n4\n\n\nTotal Sum\n \n13\n\n\n\nThe total sum is 13. Hence, 13 is the output.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= n == nums.length <= 100\n1 <= nums[i] <= 1000\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def subarraySum(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1305, "char_start": 1278, "quote": "Inpu